{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01T4JNM249BD9nBEa9pXsnfu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's a grounded summary of the **portfolio-program** planning trio session, drawn from `DESCRIPTION.md` (frozen North Star) and `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` (Phase-0 Foreman handoff).\n\n## North Star & scope\n- **The program's LOCKED North Star** is a deep, self-improving skill repository where every skill carries a locked North Star, journals its own real-use experience, and is improved during \"sleep\" sessions *without drifting* â€” first end-to-end proof being a recreate-a-paper recipe reproducing the **Gelman ANOVA paper**, graded on architecture/handoff success, *not* reproduction fidelity.\n- **This plan is Phase 0 only** â€” the shared infrastructure every skill cycle reuses. The cognitive skills (Gandalf, Ramanujan, lit-review, data-analysis, ML-code, code-verification), the recreate-a-paper proof, and the NS1 demo are each their *own* researchPrimeâ†’Crucibleâ†’Foreman cycle, not waves here.\n- **Provenance:** forged by researchPrime (engine-verified Phase-0 research) â†’ Crucible (Stage 0 lock â†’ Stage 1 Master Plan v4, 3 Shark-Tank rounds to convergence â†’ Stage 2). Frozen design is `crucible/MASTER-PLAN.md` v4.\n\n## Design pillars (locked)\n- **PRINCIPLE-D:** the no-regression GATE is deterministic-only; all LLM/cross-family judging is advisory and isolated from the terminal Foreman gate.\n- **EXECUTE/GATE trust model (FIX-16â€²):** because Foreman discards sub-agent transcripts and records no session id/artifact hash, the plan does *not* try to prove \"an LLM genuinely ran.\" Every deterministic guarantee rests on two forgery-resistant artifacts the orchestrator OWNS: (a) the TAP gate result of `node --test` (run by the orchestrator, not a sub-agent), and (b) a post-execute test-file content-hash baseline (a sub-agent can't later alter the tests it's graded by).\n- **Two-tier repo:** append-only journal vs. curated SKILL.md; eval-gated, versioned, rollback-able promotion.\n- **Persona = method + LOGICAL model tier** â€” a swappable brain seam so a different model can be dropped in later.\n- **North-Star anti-drift gate:** non-goals are machine-checkable negative canaries; a revision advancing a non-goal is rejected.\n\n## Phase-0 wave sequence (6 contiguous waves, each TAP-gated by `node --test test/`)\n- **Wave 1** â€” Eval-harness go/no-go spike + test-harness bootstrap: prove a wrapped validator emits real TAP `ok N`, a prose-deliverable path beats the vacuous-green guard, and an unreachable advisory host leaves the gate GREEN. NO-GO fallback recorded (validators as a standalone Node process via `test-command`).\n- **Wave 2** â€” Three pluggable validators as TAP emitters: schema+path-existence, deterministic canary eval, numeric-tolerance grader; advisory cross-family judge isolated (FIX-15) so its exit/stdout never reach the gate.\n- **Wave 3** â€” Machine-checkable handoff-contract gate (NS5): gates on schema-valid + all `artifact_refs` resolve on disk + `north_star` round-trips byte-identical + `open_questions` empty; wired into Anchor's HANDOFF/NEXT-PROMPT and Crucible's locate-plan path.\n- **Wave 4** â€” Per-skill repo skeleton + net-new logical-tierâ†’model table + swap test (proves swapping the table changes the resolved model with zero skill-prose edits; pinned to a model-respecting gemini-cli backend so the test isn't vacuous).\n- **Wave 5** â€” 7-field journal schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop (cluster â†’ cross-context-corroborated distill â†’ North-Star gate â†’ eval gate â†’ versioned promote with git rollback), TAP-tested on FIXTURE journals (real skills don't exist yet). Rejects non-goal-advancing lessons, blocks canary-regressing promotions (rollback), and refuses same-context-only corroboration (requires cross-context, R5).\n- **Wave 6** â€” Foundry governance wiring + canary versioning + citation hygiene: `map.json` records c